From: OpenATV RetroGaming Team <noreply@openatv.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mali-fbdev: force GLES2 on HiSilicon CV200

The CV200 Mali-T720 advertises GLES 3.1 but its STB composition path is only
reliable through GLES2, matching the separate STB-Kodi CV200 backend. Do not
query EGL surface geometry here: the legacy MV200 Mali-450 blob crashes on
its first swap after eglQuerySurface.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenATV HiSilicon vendor EGL ABI]
---
 gfx/drivers_context/mali_fbdev_ctx.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gfx/drivers_context/mali_fbdev_ctx.c b/gfx/drivers_context/mali_fbdev_ctx.c
--- a/gfx/drivers_context/mali_fbdev_ctx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers_context/mali_fbdev_ctx.c
@@ -356,4 +356,15 @@ static bool gfx_ctx_mali_fbdev_bind_api(void *data,
    unsigned version = major * 100 + minor;
+#ifdef HAVE_HISI_CV200
+   /* CV200's Mali-T720 advertises GLES 3.1 but its STB composition path is
+    * only reliable with the GLES2 renderer, matching the Kodi backend. */
+   if (version >= 300)
+   {
+      RARCH_LOG("[Mali] HiSilicon CV200: forcing the GLES2 renderer path.\n");
+      version = 200;
+   }
+#endif
    if (version >= 300)
       mali_flags |= GFX_CTX_MALI_FBDEV_FLAG_GLES3;
+   else
+      mali_flags &= ~GFX_CTX_MALI_FBDEV_FLAG_GLES3;
    return (api == GFX_CTX_OPENGL_ES_API);
-- 
